@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Shipped              |
+
+Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.
+
+## Validation at execute time
+
+- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the full missing property path as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: returns a required-property rejection without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L6), [validated by: names the full path for a nested required property rejection](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L29), [validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
+- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: reports the failing property path for a wrong-typed input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L55), [validated by: describes a wrong-typed field without echoing its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L79), [validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
+- A validation rejection is logged with the failing field path and constraint, without logging the rejected property value ([validated by: logs rejected paths and constraints without logging the rejected value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L260)).
+- Property paths in validation rejections preserve JSON Schema property names, including names that require JSON Pointer escaping ([validated by: preserves escaped property names in validation paths](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L215), [validated by: preserves escaped property names at nested validation paths](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L234)).
+- When `input` supplies a value outside a property's declared `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and the enum constraint without invoking the executor ([validated by: reports an enum rejection with its field path and constraint](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L98)).
+- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid input and undeclared properties through unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L117), [validated by: does not apply schema defaults or coerce values before execution](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L142)).
+- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake ([validated by: throws for an unregistered tool name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L142)).
+
+## Schema compilation and caching
+
+- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: reuses a static schema validator across execute calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L148)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: validates each function-valued schema against the definition current at that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L175)).
+
+## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery
+
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
